/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 68 0 R
/T (This report presents a point-in-time, source-code-focused security assessment of the NewEra \(NEA\) token contract, based solely on the materials supplied by the project team and enumerated in the scope section. It is a technical review and does not constitute financial, investment, legal, or tax advice, nor a recommendation to buy, hold, or sell any asset.)
/E (This report presents a point-in-time, source-code-focused security assessment of the NewEra \(NEA\) token contract, based solely on the materials supplied by the project team and enumerated in the scope section. It is a technical review and does not constitute financial, investment, legal, or tax advice, nor a recommendation to buy, hold, or sell any asset.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 68 0 R
/T (The NewEra contract is a minimal ERC-20 token that inherits its core behaviour from the OpenZeppelin ERC20 and Ownable libraries and adds a very small amount of custom logic: a public supply constant, a constructor that mints a fixed supply, and a holder-only burn function. The custom attack surface is therefore small.)
/E (The NewEra contract is a minimal ERC-20 token that inherits its core behaviour from the OpenZeppelin ERC20 and Ownable libraries and adds a very small amount of custom logic: a public supply constant, a constructor that mints a fixed supply, and a holder-only burn function. The custom attack surface is therefore small.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (The single Solidity source file for the NewEra contract, as supplied by the project team \(reproduced in Appendix A\). The custom logic declared in that contract: the INITIAL_SUPPLY constant, the constructor, and the burn function. The declared inheritance from OpenZeppelin ERC20 and Ownable, at the interface/behaviour level.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
