267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Based on the source code and deployment information reviewed within the defined scope, no Critical, High, or Medium severity vulnerabilities were identified in the custom NewEra contract code. This conclusion follows from the specific properties of the code: the supply is fixed and minted once, with no post-deployment minting path; transfers, approvals, and balances are inherited unchanged from OpenZeppelin with no fee, tax, blacklist, pause, or cap; the owner role confers no token-level authority; there are no external calls, no delegate calls, and no upgradeability; and arithmetic is compiler-checked.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
